---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  
  <div class="flex justify-evenly">
    <div class="mb-5">
      <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">About Me</div>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" href="/CV_JGLG_JULIO_2024_ENG3.pdf" download="CV_JGLG_JULIO_2024_ENG3.pdf">
      <button class="">
            Download CV
      </button>    
    </a>    
  </div> 

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    I have strong emotional intelligence and strategic and empathetic leadership abilities. I am capable of maintaining a positive and calm attitude during challenging situations, allowing me to analyze the situation accurately without becoming stressed. I am always seeking to acquire new knowledge and reinforce the skills I have already obtained.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement title="CONTROL AND AUTOMATION ENGINEER"  subtitle="2015 to 2019 at Instituto Politecnico Nacional, ESIME Zacatenco, CDMX, México">
        <div>
        <p class="font-normal">During my degree, I gained knowledge in industrial instrumentation, 
        with a specialization in digital control. I simulated with mathematical models, focusing on the following engineering fields:</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Control, instrumentation, and communication of process sensors, actuators, and controllers of the top brands E&H, Emerson, ABB, Allied Telesis.</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Understanding current standard processes and their safety measures based on process nature of standard regulations on intrinsically Safe protections, Nema, Ip, API processes, ISO, ISA..</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Interpretation and creation of technical drawings, engineering documents, electrical diagrams, and control diagrams such as P&ID.</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Programming and connection using industrial protocols for Allen-Bradley systems, using programs such as RSlogix and TiaPortal, for various modular equipment and frequency drives (Ethernet IP, Control-Net, Device-Net)</p>
        </div>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement title="MACHINE AND TOOLS TECHNICIAN" subtitle="2012 to 2015 at CECyT 9 Juan de Dios Batiz Paredez, CDMX, Mexico">
      <div>
        <p class="font-normal">During my time in this technical career, I have learned to:</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Operate Machinery: Lathes
                          Milling machines
                          Sanders
                          CNC machines, including programming in FANUC</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Study Material Hardness: Analyze the hardness of materials and their applicability in various contexts</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Design Mechanical Parts: Design mechanical parts and ensure their correct use.</p>
        <p class="py-2">•	Conduct Electrical Power Simulations: Perform electrical power simulations to ensure system efficiency and reliability</p>
        </div>
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>


  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
          title="Oracle - Cloud Support Engineer, OCI Networking"
          subtitle="From December 2024 to present"
      >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <img src="/oracle.svg" alt="Oracle logo" class="w-48 rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-white p-4" />
        <div class="grow min-w-[16rem]">
          <p>
            Cloud Support Engineer specialized in OCI Networking, focused on diagnosing and resolving complex connectivity, routing, VPN, FastConnect, load balancing, DNS, and network security issues. I work with enterprise customers, logs, metrics, packet captures, TCP/IP troubleshooting, and cross-functional escalations with engineering teams.
          </p>
          <a href="/blog/oracle">
            <button class="justify-end rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500 px-5 py-3 text-base mt-3 mb-3 font-medium text-red-500 transition duration-200 hover:bg-red-600/5 active:bg-red-700/5">
                Go to Full description
            </button>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
          title="Rackspace - Support Technician"
          subtitle="From April 2024 to July 2024 at Rackspace, CDMX, México"
      >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap">
        <p class="">
          In this role, I worked as part of the frontline customer support team, handling incoming customer queries with dedication and thorough analysis. I identified and resolved issues by conducting in-depth investigations, ensuring I fully understood the nature of the problems, even when they were unfamiliar. My commitment to providing accurate and relevant information often led me to research extensively before offering solutions or escalating issues through the appropriate channels.
          I also manage ticket queues effectively, ensuring that assignments are timely and directed to the appropriate technicians or teams. By coordinating tasks between departments through precise ticket routing, I minimize false alerts and significantly enhance the accuracy of our system monitoring. This proactive approach not only resolves customer issues efficiently but also strengthens overall operational reliability.
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/rackspace">
          <button class="justify-end rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500 px-5 py-3 text-base mb-3 font-medium text-red-500 transition duration-200 hover:bg-red-600/5 active:bg-red-700/5">
              Go to Full description  
          </button>    
        </a>
      </div>       
    </TimeLineElement>
    
    
    <TimeLineElement
    title="Intelite - Proposal Engineer"
    subtitle="From June 2023 to March 2024 at Intelite, CDMX, México">
      <div class="">
        <p class="">
          <p class="font-normal">•	IOT Solutions :</p>
          <p class="py-1">•	Propose and program integrated controllers for smart homes and buildings (BMS).</p>
          <p class="py-1">•	Ensure the integration and compatibility of proposed systems with existing and future infrastructures.</p>
          <p class="py-1">•	Coordinate with suppliers and contractors to ensure that components and services meet project standards and requirements.</p>
          <p class="py-1">•	Offer technical support and troubleshoot issues related to controllers, and systems.</p>
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/intelite">
          <button class="justify-end rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500 px-5 py-3 text-base mb-3 font-medium text-red-500 transition duration-200 hover:bg-red-600/5 active:bg-red-700/5">
              Go to Full description  
          </button>    
        </a>
      </div>  
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Service Engineer - IOSA"
      subtitle="From November 2022 to June 2023 at Ingenieria Operativa, CDMX, Mexico"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap">
        <p class="">
          Responsible for preventive and corrective maintenance of X-ray machines, signal blockers, walk-through metal detector arches, and narcotics and explosives detection equipment across Mexico. For at least one year, I managed approximately 45 machines at Mexico City International Airport Terminal 1 and Terminal 2, reaching around 98% operability, supporting contract compliance, avoiding penalties, and maintaining a close technical relationship with ANAM.
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/iosa">
          <button class="justify-end rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500 px-5 py-3 text-base mb-3 font-medium text-red-500 transition duration-200 hover:bg-red-600/5 active:bg-red-700/5">
              Go to Full description  
          </button>    
        </a>
      </div>
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="ATAV - Programmer and Field Engineer"
      subtitle="From February 2020 to November 2023 at Ambientes Tactiles, CDMX, Mexico"
    >
      <div class="flex flex-wrap">
        <p class="">
          I worked as a programmer and field engineer for residential and commercial automation projects, mainly with Control4 and complementary systems such as Dahua, Lutron, lighting, audio, cameras, shades, and other integrated smart devices. Unlike my later proposal engineering role at Intelite, this position was focused on field implementation, commissioning, programming, troubleshooting, and direct customer support during project delivery.
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/atav">
          <button class="justify-end rounded-xl border-2 border-red-500 px-5 py-3 text-base mb-3 font-medium text-red-500 transition duration-200 hover:bg-red-600/5 active:bg-red-700/5">
              Go to Full description  
          </button>    
        </a>
      </div> 
  </TimeLineElement>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Certifications</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 grid-cols-1">
    <li>
      <a href="#" target="_blank"> Fullstack Web Development</a>
      <div data-iframe-width="150" data-iframe-height="270" data-share-badge-id="7fa21e80-c0e7-407f-953f-e0e910557f2c" data-share-badge-host="https://www.credly.com"></div><script type="text/javascript" async src="//cdn.credly.com/assets/utilities/embed.js"></script>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/DiplomadoCanvas.jpeg" target="_blank"> Canvas Tools
        <img src="/DiplomadoCanvas.jpeg" alt="" class="flex justify-center size-60">
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/LiderazgoLaboral.jpeg" target="_blank"> Liderazgo Laboral
        <img src="/LiderazgoLaboral.jpeg" alt="" class="flex justify-center size-60">
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/KardexCursoLaboral.jpeg" target="_blank"> Kardex Liderazgo Laboral
        <img src="/KardexCursoLaboral.jpeg" alt="" class="flex justify-center size-60">
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Software</div>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc md:columns-5 columns-2 mx-6">
    <li>C++</li>
    <li>AutoDesk</li>
    <li>Office 365</li>
    <li>LabView</li>
    <li>Matlab</li>
    <li>TiaPortal</li>
    <li>RSlogix</li>
    <li>JavaScript</li>
    <li>SQL</li>
    <li>NoSQL MongoDB</li>
    <li>HTML5</li>
    <li>GCP</li>
    <li>Node.js</li>
    <li>Python</li>
    <li>Excel</li>
    <li>DNS</li>
    <li>AWS Services</li>
    <li>Windows/Linux servers</li>
    <li>Sass</li>
    <li>Git</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
